Use the native provider inventory for libc probes that cannot link.

CMake's static-library cross probes accept undeclared or unavailable
functions. This selects Windows-only _fseeki64/_ftelli64 and prevents the
normal fseeko path from compiling. These thirteen probe functions are absent
from the qualified native providers; retain every actually exported API,
including fork and posix_spawn, rather than inventing process stubs.

Upstream: PS5 native libc capability configuration only.

